und mb-2\",\"children\":\"$$175,000 After Tax in California\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3\",\"children\":\"California's progressive tax (1%–13.3%) takes a big bite. On $175,000, your net pay is $118,522 ($9,877/month). California's standard deduction for single filers is $6,083.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between text-xs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-medium\",\"children\":[\"$$118,522\",\"/yr\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"href\":\"/california-tax-calculator\",\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground hover:text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"Open Calculator →\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5 hover:border-emerald-500/30 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"$$175,000 After Tax in New York\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3\",\"children\":\"New York state tax ranges 4%–10.9%. On $175,000, take-home is $121,433 ($10,119/month). NYC residents pay an additional 3.078%–3.876% city tax on top.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between text-xs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-medium\",\"children\":[\"$$121,433\",\"/yr\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"href\":\"/new-york-tax-calculator\",\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground hover:text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"Open Calculator →\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5 hover:border-emerald-500/30 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"$$175,000 After Tax in Florida\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3\",\"children\":\"Florida has no state income tax. On $175,000, you take home $130,879 per year. Florida's average property tax is just 0.86%, and there's a homestead exemption for primary residences.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between text-xs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-medium\",\"children\":[\"$$130,879\",\"/yr\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"href\":\"/florida-tax-calculator\",\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground hover:text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"Open Calculator →\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5 hover:border-emerald-500/30 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"$$175,000 After Tax in Illinois\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3\",\"children\":\"Illinois has a flat 4.95% income tax. On $175,000, take-home is $122,353 ($10,196/month). Illinois has high property taxes averaging 1.78%, which can offset income-tax savings.\"}],\"$L28\"]}],\"$L29\"]}]]}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":[\"How We Calculate \",\"$$175,000\",\" After Taxes\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Our \",\"$$175,000\",\" after-tax calculation follows three steps:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"1\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Federal income tax\"}],\" — We apply the 2026 progressive brackets (10%, 12%, 22%, 24%, 32%, 35%, 37%) after subtracting the $16,100 standard deduction for single filers. On \",\"$$175,000\",\", your federal tax is\",\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$30,734\"}],\".\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"2\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"FICA payroll tax\"}],\" — Social Security is 6.2% on the first $184,500 of wages, plus 1.45% Medicare on all wages. Above $200,000, an additional 0.9% Medicare surtax applies. On \",\"$$175,000\",\", FICA totals\",\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$13,388\"}],\".\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"3\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"State income tax\"}],\" — We apply each state's specific brackets. For \",\"$$175,000\",\", this ranges from $0 (Texas, Florida, Washington, Nevada, etc.) up to \",\"$$12,356\",\" (California).\"]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4\",\"children\":[\"The result is your \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground\",\"children\":\"net annual take-home pay\"}],\", which we also break down into monthly, bi-weekly, and weekly amounts. These figures assume single filing status with the standard deduction and no pre-tax contributions (401(k), HSA, etc.). Use our full\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"href\":\"/paycheck-calculator\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:underli